    explanation="eng: a rolling polynomial checksum, seeded and reduced modulo a bound, that separates two strings differing in one character. math: the same fold shape IS Horner's rule -- multiply the accumulator by the base, add the new digit -- and it works at any base. cs: the fold form and the string->list form give the same count, but only the fold avoids allocating the intermediate list.",
